MADIUN REGENCY GOVERNMENT

MADIUN REGENCY GOVERNMENT

COPY

REGIONAL REGULATION OF MADIUN REGENCY

NUMBER 5 OF 2008

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF MADIUN,

Considering : a. that until now the number of violence against women and children is still high, while services and protection have not been carried out optimally;

b. that based on the consideration as referred to in letter a, it is deemed necessary to regulate the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence stipulated by Regional Regulation of Madiun Regency.

In View Of : 1. Law Number 12 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within the Province of East Java (State Gazette of 1950 Number 19, Supplement to State Gazette Number 9);

2. Law Number 6 of 1974 concerning Basic Provisions for Social Welfare (State Gazette of 1974 Number 53, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3039);

3. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3134);

4. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3668);

5. Law Number 23 of 1992 concerning Health (State Gazette of 1992 Number 100, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3495);

6. Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 138 concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (State Gazette of 1999 Number 56, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3835);

7. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3886);

8. Law Number 1 of 2000 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 182 concerning the Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labour (State Gazette of 2000 Number 30, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3941);

9. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4235);

10. Law Number 10 of 2004 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of 2004 Number 53, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4389);

11. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4419);

12. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4437) as amended by Law Number 8 of 2005 (State Gazette of 2005 Number 108, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4548);

13. Law Number 33 of 2004 concerning Financial Balance between Central Government and Regional Government (State Gazette of 2004 Number 126, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4438);

14. Government Regulation Number 6 of 1988 concerning Coordination of Vertical Agency Activities in the Regions (State Gazette of 1988 Number 10, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3373);

15. Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning Division of Government Affairs (State Gazette of 2007 Number 82, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4737);

16. Presidential Decree Number 36 of 1990 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Rights of the Child;

17. Presidential Decree Number 88 of 2002 concerning National Action Plan (RAN) for the Elimination of Trafficking in Women and Children;

18. Presidential Decree Number 61 of 2003 concerning National Action Plan for Human Rights of Indonesia 1998-2003;

19. Regional Regulation of East Java Province Number 9 of 2005 concerning Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of 2005 Number 4 Series E);

20. Regional Regulation of Madiun Regency Number 1 of 2006 concerning Medium-Term Regional Development Plan of Madiun Regency Year 2006 – 2009 (Regional Gazette of 2006 Number 1 Series E).

21. Regional Regulation of Madiun Regency Number 2 of 2008 concerning Government Affairs Under the Authority of Madiun Regency (Regional Gazette of 2008 Number 1 Series E);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF MADIUN REGENCY and

THE REGENT OF MADIUN

DECIDE

To Enact : REGIONAL REGULATION OF MADIUN REGENCY CONCERNING IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

Article 12

(1) Any person who intentionally fails to provide protection to women and children thereby causing violence, allows the occurrence of violence, and or fails to report and fails to provide protection to victims, shall be subject to sanctions as stipulated in the applicable laws and regulations;

(2) Officials appointed to organize protection who do not carry out their obligations and responsibilities shall be subject to administrative actions or sanctions; (3) PPT managers who carry out service duties that violate service principles may be subject to sanctions in accordance with the internal mechanisms of PPT.

Article 8

(1) Forms of services for victims organized by PPT include a. medical services, in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of victims carried out by medical and paramedical personnel;

b. medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service for the purposes of evidence in the legal field;

c. psychosocial services constitute services provided by companions in order to restore the traumatic condition of victims, including the provision of safe houses to protect victims from threats and intimidation for victims and provide social support so that victims have self-confidence, strength, and independence in resolving their problems;

d. legal services to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process; e. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.

(2) The service mechanism as referred to in paragraph (1) is organized according to standard operational procedures which will be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 7

(1) The organization of protection for victims is carried out in an integrated manner within the PPT framework;

(2) Provisions concerning PPT will be further regulated in the Regent Regulation.

